---
kind: scene
id: routine.morning
title: Morning readings
on: slotStart
once: false
priority: 10
when: "run.slot == 'morning'"
---

## The deck

::bg{location="deck" time="morning"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: Your {{run.day:ordinalWord}} morning, a {{clock.weekdayLabel}}. The anemometer cups are already spinning.

// clock.weekday: 0 = Monday … 6 = Sunday.
<match subject="clock.weekday">
  <when is="0">
    @narrator{code="0020"}: The log is clean and the pencil is sharp.
  </when>
  <when is="1|4">
    @narrator{code="0030"}: Post day. Somewhere below the switchbacks the postbus is grinding up in first gear.
  </when>
  <when is="2|3">
    @narrator{code="0040"}: Midweek. The station has stopped feeling new and started feeling like yours.
  </when>
  <when is="5">
    @narrator{code="0050"}: Tomorrow the village hangs its lanterns, or does not.
  </when>
  <when is="6">
    @narrator{code="0060"}: Even the barometer seems to sleep in.
  </when>
</match>

::use{component="reading" hour="Seven o'clock" instance="use-001"}

<branch id="care" prompt="The log waits, pencil in its spine.">
  <choice id="careful" text="Take the readings again, slowly, and write them exactly">
    ::set{run.readings += 1}
    @narrator{code="0070"}: You read every dial twice. Your numbers go into the column in your smallest handwriting.
  </choice>
  <choice id="skim" text="Jot them down and go find breakfast">
    @narrator{code="0080"}: Close enough. The sky won't mind a rounded decimal. Ines might.
  </choice>
</branch>
